              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CHEESYBUNNY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed this up a little.\r\n\r\nMy ingredients are as follows:\r\nFried egg\r\nToasted rye bread\r\nExtra sharp white cheddar cheese\r\nBacon (tasty addition)\r\nMayo (no ketchup)\r\n\r\nI would have liked to add tomato and onion if I had it.\r\n\r\nTraditional is good too though the way I made them before was just with egg and mayo."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rebecca Ames"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added onions, garlic and chopped fresh rosemary to the butter and cooked them together before adding the eggs. I also cooked the eggs with herbed salt and pepper. It was fantastic and easy as promised! Served as an open face sandwich on toast, with parsley and blood oranges.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-02T13:38:36.103Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mandy Rodriguez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of my favorite breakfasts to eat. It was quick to make and so delicious. I'm not big on ketchup so I didn't use it. Instead I used a slice of sharp cheddar cheese (or pepper jack cheese) and I placed the eggs over the cheese so that it can melt faster. If you love spiciness then you can add some hot sauce, jalapeños diced up or even sprinkle some cayenne pepper over the eggs. If your not into that, bacon will never fail you. Enjoy!",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-24T15:40:41.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joyce Feltz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A fried egg sandwich is the easiest comfort breakfast to be found anywhere. They are best done at home, because they cost almost nothing, and you can make them exactly how you want. I like to break the yolk and flip so I get yolk throughout. No one can cook me a fried egg sandwich as well as I can. Mayonnaise is a a must for me! To other, this may seem odd,,,but, who cares about their opinions?",
            "datePublished": "2024-03-19T22:06:28.046Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "StuKin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good combination, but not the least bit imaginative. I don't understand why so many people don't like the mayo/ketchup combination... it's called Russian dressing, and it's been around since I was a little kid (90 years ago.) This works great served on one of my home-made pitas that I make every week on the outside gas grill. The essential addition is the habanero pepper sauce I make every year.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-25T15:17:55.403Z"
          },
